preConditionHook:
// The close sits within midpointFraction of the range height either side of
// the N-bar range's midpoint. Brooks uses it NEGATED: do not take a stop entry
// in the middle of a trading range, where the fill is bad in both directions.
// At 0.17 the admitted band is the middle third of the range.
//
// Not the negation of RangeExtremeFade / CloseInRangePosition: that rule's
// negation on the long side still admits the top of the range, while this
// excludes both extremes at once.
//
// Both loops mirror EasyLanguage's Extremes(), which Highest()/Lowest() call:
// seeded at bar 0, scanning bars 1..Length-1, strict comparison. Extremes is
// EL SOURCE, so its comparison carries the EL tolerance -- el_gt/el_lt, as in
// Breakout (the reference).
rangeHigh = high[0];
rangeLow = low[0];
for (int i = 1; i < (int)rangeLookback; ++i) {
    if (el_gt(high[i], rangeHigh)) rangeHigh = high[i];
    if (el_lt(low[i], rangeLow)) rangeLow = low[i];
}
rangeMid = (rangeHigh + rangeLow) / 2;
